Third-party material
--------------------

This crate embeds trust material published by the Mozilla Foundation as
part of the Mozilla Root Store, and redistributes it under the same
license Mozilla applies to that material in NSS.

  Root certificates, trust bits, and applied constraints
    Common CA Database (CCADB), operated by Mozilla on Salesforce.
    https://ccadb.my.salesforce-sites.com/mozilla/IncludedRootCertificateReportPEMCSV
    Snapshot: 2026-08-13, 172 included roots.
    Embedded at roots/mozilla/*.der and src/generated.rs.

  Intermediate CA certificates (feature `mozilla_cas`)
    Common CA Database (CCADB).
    https://ccadb.my.salesforce-sites.com/mozilla/PublicAllIntermediateCertsWithPEMCSV
    https://ccadb.my.salesforce-sites.com/mozilla/MozillaIntermediateCertsCSVReport
    Embedded at cas/mozilla/*.der and cas/mozilla/mozilla.cbor.

  Cross-check source
    NSS lib/ckfw/builtins/certdata.txt, licensed MPL-2.0, is the
    authoritative expression of the same root store. tools/verify_against_nss.py
    checks the embedded certificates and trust bits against it.
    https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nss-dev/nss/master/lib/ckfw/builtins/certdata.txt

The individual root and intermediate certificates are the works of the
certification authorities that issued them. Mozilla's contribution, and
what this crate reproduces, is the selection of those certificates and
the trust decisions recorded beside them.

CCADB publishes its reports under its own data usage terms, which are
separate from and additional to the MPL-2.0 terms above. See
https://www.ccadb.org/ for those terms.


Files that cannot carry a license header
----------------------------------------

The DER certificates under roots/mozilla/ and cas/mozilla/, and the CBOR
store cas/mozilla/mozilla.cbor, are binary and cannot carry the Exhibit A
notice in the file itself. As MPL-2.0 Exhibit A permits, the notice is
placed where a recipient would look for it: README.md in each of those
directories, and this file.
